      "message": "It\u0027s off by one. There are 16 ARM exception vectors, then the Cr50\u0027s SoC defines hardware interrupts 0..N, and then GC_INTERRUPTS_COUNT is defined as N + 16.\n\nBut there are actually N + 17 interrupts, because the interrupt numbering starts with 0. \n\n(GC_INTERRUPTS_COUNT + 1) - 16 \u003d\u003d GC_INTERRUPTS_COUNT - 15, which is the value that CONFIG_IRQ_COUNT should have.",
